(FLW-03: `But if <condition> then,` is an else-if arm; arms are tested in
 order, the first match wins, and `Otherwise` catches the rest.
 Also covers FLW-07: the periods before `But if` and `Otherwise` do NOT
 end the sentence - if they did, the score-2 run would also print "many".
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox FLW-03.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   two
   many
)
a number called score is 2.
If score is 1 then, print "one". But if score is 2 then, print "two". Otherwise, print "many".
a number called other is 9.
If other is 1 then, print "one". But if other is 2 then, print "two". Otherwise, print "many".
